FAQ = [
 ("What is the best tonneau cover for a 2022+ Nissan Frontier?",
  "For most owners, the BAKFlip MX4 (448538 for the 5 ft bed). It has aluminum panels with polymer cores, a 400 lb distributed load rating, auto-latching, a 5-year warranty and a click-in install BAK quotes at 30 minutes or less. RealTruck lists it at $1,049.99. If your truck has the Utili-track channels, confirm on the listing that your version covers them, or choose a cover that states it works with or without Utili-track, like the UnderCover Select or the Extang Endure ALX."),
 ("Do 2005–2021 Frontier tonneau covers fit a 2022 Frontier?",
  "Don't assume they do. The makers on this page sell separate 2022+ parts: RetraxPRO MX 80721 is listed for 2005–2021 and 80731 for 2022+, the BAKFlip MX4 is 448506 against 448538, and the Tyger T3 is TG-BC3N1028 against TG-BC3N1057. The older covers are listed for a 4'11\" (58.6 in) bed, and the 2022+ parts for a 5' (59.5–60 in) bed. The 2022 truck kept a revised version of the old frame, and some sellers blur the two generations. Buy the 2022+ part number."),
 ("Why do so many listings still say 2005–2021 or 2005–2025?",
  "The 2022 Frontier kept a revised version of the D40 ladder frame, and the 5 ft bed name carried over, and some marketplace sellers list one cover across both generations. One unbranded FRP tri-fold, for example, is titled for 2005–2025 Frontiers with a 5 ft (59.5 in) bed. That may be fine or it may leave a gap. The brands that engineer each generation separately list different part numbers, which tells you the fit changed. When a listing spans 2005 to today, ask the seller to confirm 2022+ fit in writing."),
 ("How do I know if I have the 5 ft or 6 ft bed?",
  "Crew Cab trucks come with the 5 ft bed or the 6 ft long bed; King Cab trucks have the 6 ft bed. Cover listings print the short bed as 5' (59.5 or 60 in) and the long bed as 6' or 6'1\" (72.25 to 73.3 in, depending on the maker). If you are not sure, measure inside the bed at the rail from the bulkhead to the closed tailgate, then order the part number the maker lists for that length."),
 ("What is Utili-track and does it affect tonneau cover fit?",
  "Utili-track is Nissan's channel system for sliding tie-down cleats. Nissan describes the current Frontier's bed as having three available Utili-track channels, and some trims include it with two adjustable cleats. The channels sit where clamp-on covers attach, so every listing worth buying says whether it fits trucks with Utili-track, without it, or both. The UnderCover Select, Extang Endure ALX, RetraxPRO XR and Tyger T3 on this page all state they fit with or without it."),
 ("Hard or soft cover — which is better on a Frontier?",
  "Hard covers (MX4, Endure ALX, UnderCover Select, RetraxPRO XR) lock under a locked tailgate and carry 300–500 lb spread evenly. Soft covers (TruXedo Pro X15, Tyger T3) cost $223–$550, weigh less and come off quickly, but a knife gets through fabric or vinyl. Buy hard if tools or bikes stay in the bed overnight. Buy soft if you mostly want to keep weather and road dirt out and value easy removal."),
 ("Can I carry cargo or a rooftop tent on a Frontier tonneau cover?",
  "Only on hard covers, and only up to the published evenly distributed rating: 500 lb for the Extang Endure ALX and RetraxPRO XR, 400 lb for the BAKFlip MX4, and 300 lb for the UnderCover Select. Those ratings assume a flat, spread load. For a rooftop tent, crossbars or a bike mount, you need a cover with T-slot rails such as the RetraxPRO XR or BAK's MX4 TS; RealTruck notes that crossbars and accessories are sold separately."),
 ("Do I need to drill to install a cover on a Frontier?",
  "No. Every cover here clamps inside the bed rails. The makers quote 5–10 minutes for the Tyger T3, 30 minutes or less for the BAKFlip MX4 and UnderCover Select, and under an hour for the Extang Endure ALX, RetraxPRO XR and TruXedo Pro X15. Tyger notes that a bedliner that wraps over the rails needs small holes cut for the clamps. Under-rail and spray-in liners need nothing."),
 ("Is a retractable cover worth it on a mid-size truck?",
  "It is if you open the bed many times a day or want to mount racks over the bed. The RetraxPRO XR locks at any position, carries 500 lb and adds T-slot rails for crossbars. The costs are the price ($1,999.99 at RealTruck), the canister at the front of a bed that is only 5 ft long to start with, and roller service that means pulling the canister. Retrax does not publish the canister depth on this listing, so ask the seller if bulkhead space matters."),
 ("Do the covers fit the PRO-4X and other trims?",
  "Fit follows the bed, not the trim. The covers here are listed by model year and bed length, not by S, SV, SL or PRO-4X, so a PRO-4X Crew Cab with the 5 ft bed takes the same 5 ft part as an SV Crew Cab. What changes between trucks is equipment in the bed: Utili-track channels, bedliners that wrap over the rails, and bed-mounted accessories. Check those, then order by bed length."),
]

